      "createdAt": 1788393600000,
      "updatedAt": 1788393600000,
      "id": "jw-event-gate-of-ghosts",
      "chapterId": "jw-chapter-011",
      "timelineId": "jw-timeline-road",
      "title": "Judge Cui at the Gate",
      "description": "The letter is read at the gate by a judge who bows as though the court were still sitting. Then the road out of it fills with the emperor’s own dead — the brothers he killed to take the throne — and it takes a blue-faced servant with a stick to get him through them.",
