      "createdAt": 1788393600000,
      "updatedAt": 1788393600000,
      "id": "jw-event-years-altered",
      "chapterId": "jw-chapter-011",
      "timelineId": "jw-timeline-road",
      "title": "Thirteen Made Thirty-Three",
      "description": "The Ten Kings hear the dragon’s complaint and find for the emperor, because the beheading was ordered above and not by him. Then the register is fetched to see how long he has left, and the judge puts two strokes on a thirteen while the book is in his hands.",
