      "createdAt": 1788393600000,
      "updatedAt": 1788393600000,
      "id": "jw-event-the-cart-pullers",
      "chapterId": "jw-chapter-044",
      "timelineId": "jw-timeline-road",
      "title": "Five Hundred Monks on a Sand Bank",
      "description": "The roar on the road is five hundred monks in cangues hauling brick and timber up a cliff, chanting to a bodhisattva of Great Strength. Twenty years ago the rain stopped, the monks prayed and failed, and three Daoists called it down; since then the temples are pulled down, the ordination papers burnt, and the monks belong to the men who saved the harvest.",
      "locationMarkerId": "jw-location-cart-slow-kingdom",
